# trivy allowlist for the `image-scan` job (ADR-0030, as amended).
#
# One finding per line, in trivy's own syntax:  <CVE-or-GHSA-id> exp:<YYYY-MM-DD>
# preceded by a comment saying WHY it is not reachable in what ships. `exp:` is
# mandatory: trivy stops honouring the line on that date, so a suppression cannot
# outlive its review. Keep it within 90 days of adding the line (a review rule).
#
# An entry is allowed only for a finding triaged as NOT REACHABLE in the running image
# (for example, a package present only in a build stage that is not copied into the
# final one). A reachable finding is fixed, never listed here. The triage reasoning for
# each entry is kept in the private record, not in this public file.
#
# Do NOT add a line to make a red run green. Same rule as .gitleaksignore.
